---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rangeway Mojave · The First Rangeway Location"
  description="100% off-grid, solar-powered ultra-fast EV charging is coming to the CA-14 corridor in the Antelope Valley. The first Rangeway location. Coming 2027."
  image="/images/basecamp-rosamond.jpg"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The First Rangeway Location"
    title="Rangeway Mojave."
    lede="100% off-grid, solar-powered ultra-fast charging on the CA-14 corridor. Coming 2027."
    image="/images/basecamp-rosamond.jpg"
    imageAlt="Aerial view of Rangeway Mojave at dusk with solar canopy, battery storage, and charging plaza beside the highway"
    align="left"
    scrim="strong"
  >
    <div class="mojave-hero__ctas">
      <a class="btn btn-warm" href="https://mojave.rangewayev.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Visit the microsite
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
          <polyline points="13 6 19 12 13 18" />
        </svg>
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://fieldnotes.rangewayev.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Subscribe to Field Notes
      </a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow prose-lg reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why here</p>
      <h2>The Antelope Valley. 95,460 reasons.</h2>
      <p>
        The CA-14 corridor connects the Los Angeles basin to the high desert and points north. It carries 95,460 vehicles per day past the Dawn Road interchange, including the daily commute for thousands of aerospace and defense workers at Edwards Air Force Base, Northrop Grumman, Lockheed Martin, Boeing, NASA, and Virgin Galactic. On weekends, it carries travelers heading to the Eastern Sierra and beyond.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now, those drivers have nowhere premium to charge. Rangeway Mojave changes that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-cream">
    <div class="container-narrow reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Phase I</p>
      <h2>Built from the ground up. Powered by the sun.</h2>
      <p class="prose-lg">
        Phase I delivers six DC fast charging ports under a custom timber canopy, powered entirely by an on-site 990 kW ground-mounted solar array and a 3.6 MWh battery energy storage system. The entire site operates independently of the electrical grid. Engineered by <a href="https://carbondc.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Carbon DC</a>, whose off-grid platform is already operating at multiple sites across California's desert corridors.
      </p>
      <p class="prose-lg">
        Fresh food and drinks are served from our on-site Rivian EDV food truck. Desert-native landscaping and shaded seating round out the experience. Premium from the pavement up.
      </p>
      <p class="prose-lg muted">
        Phase II brings the full Rangeway experience: a 2,500 square foot climate-controlled driver's lounge with a staffed cafe, comfortable seating, premium restrooms, and on-site coffee roasting from <a href="https://redcanyonroasting.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Red Canyon Roasting Company</a>. The lounge is coming shortly after launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-muted" style="color: var(--color-warm);">Read the full story</p>
      <h2>Every network starts with one site. This is ours.</h2>
      <p class="prose-lg" style="margin-top: var(--space-5); opacity: 0.85;">
        Visit the Rangeway Mojave microsite for the full story: site stats, how the off-grid platform works, the vision behind the network, and how to follow construction progress.
      </p>
      <div style="margin-top: var(--space-7); display: flex; gap: var(--space-4); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a class="btn btn-warm" href="https://mojave.rangewayev.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Visit Rangeway Mojave
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
            <polyline points="13 6 19 12 13 18" />
          </svg>
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/network">Explore the Network</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .mojave-hero__ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
